K-quant MMQ on HIP: the sub-block scale times the dot sum as a float multiply

From llama-navi21-furnace (github.com/sixvolts/llama-navi21-furnace, b4e2700f8), ggml/src/ggml-cuda/vecdotq.cuh:
ggml_cuda_mmq_scale_sumi(sc, sumi) returns (float) sc * (float) sumi under GGML_USE_HIP, and (float) (sc * sumi), the
stock form, elsewhere.  The Q4_K / Q5_K / Q6_K MMQ and MMVQ dot helpers call it.  On AMD the 32-bit integer multiply
(v_mul_lo_u32) runs at a quarter of the rate of the float multiply.

The result is the same number: both factors and the product are integers below 2^24, which FP32 holds exactly.
  Q4_K: scale <= 63, |dot sum| <= 32 * 15 * 127 = 60960, product <= 3840480.
  Q5_K: scale <= 63, |dot sum| <= 32 * 31 * 127 = 125984, product <= 7936992.
  Q6_K: |scale| <= 128, |dot sum| <= 16 * 32 * 127 = 65024 per half, the two products summed <= 16646144 (2^24 = 16777216).
tests/hip/prefill_kquant_parity.cpp runs blocks of exactly these largest values (its "raw" case).

Base: llama.cpp 3cf03257f219afbe7334045ff7c6a06ac68c627d (third_party/ggml/VERSION.txt).
Apply:  patch -p1 -d third_party/llama.cpp < third_party/llama.cpp-patches/0001-kquant-mmq-fp32-scale-multiply.patch
Remove: the same with -R (after 0002 is removed, or leave 0002: the two do not overlap).

--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/vecdotq.cuh
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/vecdotq.cuh
@@ -501,6 +501,17 @@
